WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.840
It’s crazy when you think about all of
the different kinds of foods we eat.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:09.760
We just swallow and hope
it all works out for the best.

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.280
Well, as it turns out,

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.680
there are better ways to think about keeping
our bodies humming healthfully along.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.080
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast,

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:21.280
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:23.840
Today, we look at the
health effects of food additives.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:25.360
And in our first story,

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:30.560
NutritionFacts Senior Research
Scientist Dr. Kristine Dennis asks

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:35.120
‘Do the reactions ascribed to
monosodium glutamate (MSG)

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:39.200
represent a menace, myth, or marvel?’

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.360
Reducing sodium intake
by 30 percent

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:44.800
could save the lives
of more than 40 million people.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:46.960
And guess what can reduce
sodium intake

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:50.320
by more than 30 percent
in standard recipes?

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:53.920
Substituting traditional salt
with monosodium glutamate,

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:57.040
commonly known as MSG.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:59.360
But what about "Chinese
Restaurant Syndrome,"

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.120
reported in a 1968 letter

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.280
to the New England
Journal of Medicine,

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:05.840
characterized by numbness
on the back of the neck,

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:08.400
general weakness,
and palpitation?

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.640
One of the proposed causes
was MSG,

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:14.960
a common seasoning often used
in Chinese cooking.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:16.960
Since then, MSG has been blamed

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:18.880
for causing
numerous adverse reactions,

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:23.520
including asthma, headache,
and neuropsychiatric disorders.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.720
But is this so-called
monosodium glutamate "allergy"

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:29.840
a menace or a myth?

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:32.800
You don't know
until you put it to the test,

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:34.640
or in this case, many tests.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.680
In a multicenter, double-blind,
placebo-controlled,

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:41.360
multiple-challenge trial of MSG,

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:44.480
130 self-reported
MSG-reactive volunteers

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:48.080
first consumed beverages
containing 5 grams of MSG

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:50.240
or a placebo,

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:52.320
and those who reported
two or more

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.760
of 10 different symptoms,
such as flushing or headache,

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:59.200
were then rechallenged
in a dose-response study.

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:01.680
Of the 19 people
who consistently responded

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:04.800
to 5 grams of MSG
mixed in a drink,

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.280
once MSG was given in a capsule

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:08.400
(therefore ensuring people

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.960
couldn't actually taste
the MSG,

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:13.440
which they could
when it was mixed in a drink),

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.920
only two people had reactions.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:19.600
The researchers noted that
large doses of MSG without food

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:22.240
may result in more symptoms,

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:26.320
but no persistent or serious
effects were observed.

00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:29.840
For context,
estimated MSG intakes in the UK

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.400
are about 0.58 grams per day,

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.680
and in Asian countries,

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:36.240
such as China, Korea,
and Vietnam,

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.240
where it is
a more commonly used seasoning,

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:40.800
it ranges from 0.33 grams
per day

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:43.360
to 3.8 grams per day,

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:47.280
which is generally much less
than the massive 5g or greater

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:50.560
single doses provided
in the challenge trials.

00:02:50.560 --> 00:02:53.600
Yet, only 2 out of 130 people

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.400
who claimed
to be sensitive to MSG

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.320
had any more symptoms than
when they just took a placebo.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:02.080
Given the controversy,

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:04.240
consensus meetings
with scientific experts

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:08.160
convened in 1997
and again in 2007,

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:10.640
and concluded that
MSG was harmless,

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:14.400
and no dietary intake limits
needed to be set.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:18.276
But, in 2017, the
European Food Safety Authority

00:03:18.276 --> 00:03:21.680
reevaluated the safety
of glutamate as a food additive,

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:24.160
and decided
to set a limit of 30 mg

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:27.040
per kilogram of body weight
per day,

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:30.160
which is exceeded by
most people every day.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:33.520
This limit was based off
a rat study from 1979,

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.440
with EFSA citing potential

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:39.200
neurodevelopmental
toxicity concerns.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.360
But even the author
of the original study

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:44.960
says they failed to convincingly
show such an effect.

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:48.160
And given MSG's
salt-reducing benefits,

00:03:48.160 --> 00:03:51.120
might it be a-okay
as a much-needed tool

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:54.000
to reduce sodium in foods?

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.400
Now, MSG still has sodium;

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:00.000
it's monosodium glutamate,
after all;

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.680
with about one third the sodium
of typical table salt.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:07.200
So, a better salt substitute
would be potassium salt,

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:08.480
potassium chloride,

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:12.800
which has the potential
to save even more lives.

00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:16.800
Did you know the consumption of
phosphorus preservatives in junk food,

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:18.480
and injected into meat,

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.840
may damage blood vessels,
accelerate the aging process,

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:26.000
and contribute to osteoporosis?

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.360
In my video "Treating Kidney
Failure through Diet",

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:34.240
I profiled research suggesting that
the use of plant-based diet

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:38.000
may be helpful for the patients
with kidney failure,

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.320
because control of dietary
phosphorus intake

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:42.640
is the lynchpin in the
successful control

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:46.080
of a leading cause of disease and
death in kidney failure patients,

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:48.800
too much phosphorous
in the blood.

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:50.880
But now we're beginning
to realize

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:54.720
that absorbing too much phosphorus
isn't good for anyone.

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:56.880
Having high levels in our
blood has been found

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:59.200
to be an independent predictor
of heart attacks

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:02.480
and mortality in the
general population,

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.560
increasing the risk of not
only kidney failure,

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:09.840
but heart failure, heart attacks,
coronary death, and overall death.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:11.840
Higher phosphate
levels associated

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:15.200
with a significantly
shorter lifespan.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:18.240
Dietary intake of phosphate
is an important matter

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:23.280
not just for persons with kidney
disease, but for everybody.

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:26.720
It's thought to cause
damage to blood vessels

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:30.000
and accelerate the
aging process,

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.200
even potentially
hurting our bones,

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:39.760
contributing to osteoporosis by
disrupting hormonal regulation.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:42.240
The estimated average
requirement of phosphorus

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:44.320
is less than 600 a day,

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:46.320
but the estimated
average intake

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:49.600
is nearly twice that
in the United States.

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:52.240
How do we stay away
from the stuff?

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:53.760
If you look at
nutrient tables,

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:56.640
it looks like many plant foods
have as much phosphorous

00:05:56.640 --> 00:05:57.920
as many animal foods,

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:00.640
So why are plant-based
diets so effective

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:03.120
in treating kidney
failure patients?

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:06.320
Because most of the
phosphorus in plant foods

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:08.720
is found in the
form of phytic acid,

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:10.320
which we don't digest,

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:13.120
so the bioavailability
of plant phosphates

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:16.080
is usually less than 50%.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:22.960
See, only a third to a half of plant
phosphorus may be absorbable,

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:30.160
whereas most animal products
are all up around 75%.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:32.240
So when you adjust
for how much

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.240
actually gets
into our system

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:37.680
you see plant foods
are better.

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:40.800
It's like the absorption of
heme and non-heme iron,

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.120
our body can protect
itself from absorbing

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:44.720
too much plant-based iron,

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:46.880
but can't stop excess
blood-based,

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.400
or heme iron
from animals

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:51.760
slipping through
the intestinal wall.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:53.600
The worst kind
of phosphorus,

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:57.840
absorbed nearly 100%,
are phosphate additives

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:00.480
added, for example,
to cola drinks.

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:02.000
Why would they
do that?

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:05.920
Otherwise cola drinks
would be black.

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:07.520
Without the
added phosphate,

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:09.600
there would be so many
glycotoxins produced

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:12.560
that the beverage would
turn pitch black.

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:16.640
Thus, cola drinks owe their
brown color to phosphate.

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:20.640
Phosphate additives play an
especially important role

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:23.440
in the meat industry, where they
are used as preservatives,

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:28.080
for the same reason – to enhance
a meat products color.

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:31.840
Just like the dairy industry
adds aluminum to cheese,

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:34.080
meat and poultry
is "enhanced"

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:38.320
by injecting it
with phosphates.

00:07:38.320 --> 00:07:41.040
If you look at meat industry
trade journals

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:43.440
and can get past all
the macabre ads

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:46.240
for head dropping robots
for the kill floor

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:48.560
and foot chopper-offers,

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:52.560
you'll see all these ads
for injection machines.

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:54.160
Why?

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:56.720
Because of increased
profitability.

00:07:56.720 --> 00:08:01.440
Enhanced meats have better
color and less purge.

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:04.480
Purge is a term used to
describe the liquid

00:08:04.480 --> 00:08:07.280
that seeps from
flesh as it ages.

00:08:07.280 --> 00:08:09.440
Many consumers find
this unattractive

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:12.240
and so the industry
views it as a win-win.

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:15.360
When you inject chicken
with phosphates

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:18.400
the consumer benefits through
the perception of enhanced quality,

00:08:18.400 --> 00:08:22.160
and the processor benefits
from increased yield

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:24.000
because they just pumped
it up with water

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:27.680
and they sell it
by the pound.

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:33.920
The problem is that it can
boost phosphorus levels

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:37.040
in meat nearly 70%,

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:42.800
a real and insidious danger
for kidney patients,

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:47.665
but now we know it's
a danger for all.

